label(scale(0.8)*"$B$", (7.5,2.2), E);
label(scale(0.8)*"$C$", (5,0), S);
fill((0,-.8)--(1,-.8)--(1,-.95)--cycle, white);
[/asy]

solution:
Segments $\overline{AD}$ and $\overline{BE}$ are drawn perpendicular to $\overline{YZ}$.  Segments $\overline{AB}$, $\overline{AC}$ and $\overline{BC}$ divide $\triangle XYZ$ into four congruent triangles.  Vertical line segments $\overline{AD}$, $\overline{XC}$ and $\overline{BE}$ divide each of these in half.  Three of the eight small triangles are shaded, or $\frac{3}{8}$ of $\triangle XYZ$.  The shaded area is $\frac{3}{8}(8) = \boxed{3}$. [asy]
