label("$y = g(x)$", (2.2,parabtwo(2.2)), N, blue);

dot((0,0));
dot((0,-1));
dot((1,0));
dot((1,-1));
[/asy]

Therefore,
\[\frac{-\frac{a}{2} - \frac{c}{2}}{2} = 100,\]which implies $a + c = \boxed{-400}.$

