&= \boxed{5}
\end{align*}

$$\text{- OR -}$$

We wish to find $(a - 1)(b - 1) = ab - (a + b) + 1$. If $a$ and $b$ are roots of this quadratic, then Vieta's formulas give us that $ab = 9$ and $a + b = 5$. Substituting these values, we find that $(a - 1)(b - 1) = 9 - 5 + 1 = \boxed{5}$.

We begin by drawing a diagram: [asy]
size(5cm);
pair a=(0,1); pair b=(1,1); pair c=(1,0); pair d=(0,0); pair e=(1,.82); pair f=(a+e)/2; pair g=(d+e)/2;
fill(b--e--g--f--cycle,gray);
fill(g--c--d--cycle,pink);
dot(a);dot(b);dot(c);dot(d);dot(e);dot(f);dot(g);
